Patch: 010-repair-without-a-note
Reason: a call the rollout has no output for gets its output from the log whenever a thread resumes, before any turn is sent, not only under a recovery note: a turn that ended without answering a call (one interrupted mid-call, or settled instead of resumed) left it dangling, and the provider refuses a history with a call unanswered; this is the hook, the repair itself is in code-mode.ts
Upstream: ours
Pins: a crash inside a never tool's call, then the turn closed in the log: the next send answers the dangling call from the log before the new turn, and the call is never run again
Pins: a settled turn whose exec dangles with a completed never call does not answer a new turn's same call as recorded earlier: the new call runs
---
diff --git a/packages/harness-codex/src/harness.ts b/packages/harness-codex/src/harness.ts
index 436c2a9..e4f76c1 100644
--- a/packages/harness-codex/src/harness.ts
+++ b/packages/harness-codex/src/harness.ts
@@ -1051,6 +1051,8 @@ export function codexHarness(options: CodexHarnessOptions = {}): Harness {
       await driveFiles.catchUp();
       // A turn a crash cut off.
       const note = recoveryNote(ctx.state());
+      // With no recovery note, calls the rollout left unanswered still get their outputs before any turn is sent.
+      if (!note && resume) await code.repairUnnoted(lines);
       if (note) {
         const summary = summarizeRollout(lines);
         const owed = owedSubmissions(ctx.state(), note.turn.placed, summary.clientIds);
